# self_ctor_removed_err.tkr — the §4.1 `self { … }`-is-retired REJECT host. The `self { … }`
# construction form is removed (R2), so a `self { … }` in a method body no longer parses as a
# construction — the parser reads `self` as a bare receiver and then rejects the following `{`. The
# SAME file uses `self` as a RECEIVER (`self._n`) and as a return TYPE (`(): self`) without error,
# proving only the construction form was retired. It has no successful build to sanitize/run.

Feature: §4.1 `self { … }` retired — the compiler rejects a `self { … }` construction

  # (removed) a `self { … }` in a method body is a parse error now that the construction form is
  # retired; `self` as a receiver / a type in the same file stays valid.
  Scenario: removed — a `self { … }` construction is rejected as a parse error
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "after a statement"
